,"icon":235},"Grind Jobs","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fgrind-jobs","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F02.grind-jobs","i-lucide-workflow",{"title":237,"path":238,"stem":239,"icon":174},"Project Publishing Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fproject-publishing-design","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F03.project-publishing-design",{"title":241,"path":242,"stem":243,"icon":33},"Sign-In Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fsign-in-design","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F04.sign-in-design",{"title":245,"path":246,"stem":247,"icon":248},"Development Server","\u002Fplatform\u002Fdevelopment-server","04.platform\u002F13.development-server","i-lucide-server-cog",{"title":250,"path":251,"stem":252,"icon":253},"Supply Chain Security","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsupply-chain-security","04.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security","i-lucide-package-check",{"title":255,"path":256,"stem":257,"icon":258},"Enterprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","04.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":260,"title":15,"body":261,"description":515,"extension":516,"links":517,"meta":518,"navigation":519,"path":16,"seo":520,"stem":17,"__hash__":521},"docs\u002F01.getting-started\u002F02.quick-start.md",{"type":262,"value":263,"toc":511},"minimark",[264,268,481,486,489,507],[265,266,267],"p",{},"Kinotic runs on your own machine today. Kinotic OS Cloud, where Kinotic runs for you, is coming soon.",[269,270,272,474],"tabs",{"sync":271},"kinotic-install",[273,274,277,280,285,322,445],"tabs-item",{"icon":275,"label":276},"i-lucide-laptop","Local",[265,278,279],{},"The local install runs the whole of Kinotic OS in Docker on your machine: its servers, the portal, the\nGit server that holds your projects' repositories, and the storage your apps' data and UIs live in.\nNothing leaves your machine except the downloads.",[281,282,284],"h4",{"id":283},"prerequisites","Prerequisites",[286,287,288,296,302,313,319],"ul",{},[289,290,291,295],"li",{},[292,293,294],"strong",{},"Docker"," with Compose, running, with at least 12 GB of memory available to it",[289,297,298,301],{},[292,299,300],{},"Node.js"," 18 or later, which the Kinotic CLI runs on",[289,303,304,307,308,312],{},[292,305,306],{},"macOS on Apple silicon, or Linux with KVM"," (",[309,310,311],"code",{},"\u002Fdev\u002Fkvm","), where your apps' deployments run as micro VMs",[289,314,315,318],{},[292,316,317],{},"Claude Code",", which builds your app with the Kinotic plugin",[289,320,321],{},"An internet connection for the first start, which downloads Kinotic, and for each new project, whose starting code comes from GitHub",[323,324,326,330,362,388,395,399,407,411,416,434,442],"steps",{"level":325},"4",[281,327,329],{"id":328},"install-and-launch-kinotic","Install and launch Kinotic",[331,332,337],"pre",{"className":333,"code":334,"language":335,"meta":336,"style":336},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","curl -fsSL https:\u002F\u002Fkinotic.ai\u002Finstall | sh\n","bash","",[309,338,339],{"__ignoreMap":336},[340,341,344,348,352,355,359],"span",{"class":342,"line":343},"line",1,[340,345,347],{"class":346},"sBMFI","curl",[340,349,351],{"class":350},"sfazB"," -fsSL",[340,353,354],{"class":350}," https:\u002F\u002Fkinotic.ai\u002Finstall",[340,356,358],{"class":357},"sMK4o"," |",[340,360,361],{"class":346}," sh\n",[265,363,364,365,372,373,376,377,380,381,384,385,387],{},"This installs ",[366,367,371],"a",{"href":368,"rel":369},"https:\u002F\u002Fbun.sh",[370],"nofollow","Bun"," if you don't have it, installs the Kinotic CLI, adds Bun's bin\nfolder to your ",[309,374,375],{},"PATH"," in your shell's profile if it isn't there yet, and runs ",[309,378,379],{},"kinotic local up",", which\nstarts Kinotic and the node your projects deploy to. The first start downloads everything and prepares\nthe database, which takes a few minutes; the command returns once Kinotic is ready. Open a new terminal\nto use ",[309,382,383],{},"kinotic"," there. With the CLI already installed, ",[309,386,379],{}," alone starts it.",[265,389,390,391,394],{},"To update the CLI, run ",[309,392,393],{},"kinotic local down",", then the same line again.",[281,396,398],{"id":397},"create-your-organization","Create your organization",[265,400,401,402,406],{},"Open ",[366,403,404],{"href":404,"rel":405},"http:\u002F\u002Flocalhost:9090\u002Fsignup",[370],", enter your name and email, then name\nyour organization and set a password. A local install sends no email, so the page goes straight on, and\nyou are signed in to your new organization.",[281,408,410],{"id":409},"follow-the-quickstart-in-the-portal","Follow the Quickstart in the portal",[265,412,401,413,415],{},[292,414,5],{}," in the portal's sidebar. It walks you through installing the Kinotic plugin in Claude\nCode, connecting Claude to your local Kinotic, and asking for your app. Claude creates the application\nand its project, writes the entities, services and UIs, and pushes to the project's repository; every\npush deploys.",[265,417,418,419,422,423,426,427,429,430,433],{},"For local use, Claude connects to your Kinotic through ",[309,420,421],{},"kinotic-local",", the MCP server the Quickstart\nhas you add. In Claude Code's ",[309,424,425],{},"\u002Fmcp"," list, authenticate ",[309,428,421],{},". Don't worry about\n",[309,431,432],{},"plugin:kinotic:kinotic-os"," in the same list: the Kinotic plugin adds it for use with Kinotic Cloud,\nand local use doesn't need it.",[331,435,440],{"className":436,"code":438,"language":439,"meta":336},[437],"language-text","User MCPs\n❯ ⚠ kinotic-local                needs authentication    ← for local use: authenticate it\n\nBuilt-in MCPs\n  ⚠ plugin:kinotic:kinotic-os    needs authentication    ← for Kinotic Cloud: not needed locally\n","text",[309,441,438],{"__ignoreMap":336},[265,443,444],{},"If you also work on Kinotic Cloud, authenticate both: Claude works on each project through the\nserver that holds it, and asks which one to create a new app on.",[265,446,447,449,450,452,453,456,457,460,461,464,465,469,470,473],{},[309,448,393],{}," stops Kinotic and the apps it deployed, and keeps your data for the next ",[309,451,379],{},";\n",[309,454,455],{},"kinotic local down --delete-data"," deletes it. ",[309,458,459],{},"kinotic local status"," and ",[309,462,463],{},"kinotic local logs"," show what\nit is doing, and the ",[366,466,468],{"href":467},"\u002Fapps\u002Fcli-reference#kinotic-local","CLI reference"," covers each command.\n",[366,471,472],{"href":209},"Developing Kinotic"," covers how to work on Kinotic itself.",[273,475,478],{"icon":476,"label":477},"i-lucide-cloud","Cloud",[479,480],"cloud-waitlist",{},[482,483,485],"h2",{"id":484},"whats-next","What's Next?",[265,487,488],{},"Once your first app is deployed, explore the rest of the documentation:",[286,490,491,497,502],{},[289,492,493,496],{},[366,494,495],{"href":52},"Application Structure"," -- Understand how organizations, applications, projects, and artifacts are organized.",[289,498,499,501],{},[366,500,63],{"href":69}," -- Learn how to publish and consume services across your application.",[289,503,504,506],{},[366,505,84],{"href":90}," -- Dive deeper into entity definitions, relationships, and querying.",[508,509,510],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sBMFI, html code.shiki .sBMFI{--shiki-light:#E2931D;--shiki-default:#FFCB6B;--shiki-dark:#FFCB6B}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html pre.shiki code .sMK4o, html code.shiki .sMK4o{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF}html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-sty